.TH ZDOTS-USAGE 1 "2026-08-02" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
zdots-usage \- CLI usage intelligence from the local trace stream (/Users/mike.hall/.local/state/zsh/traces.jsonl).
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBzdots-usage --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
Usage: zdots-usage [report] [--days N] [--top N]

CLI usage intelligence from the local trace stream (/Users/mike.hall/.local/state/zsh/traces.jsonl).

Reports:
  summary     headline numbers from every report (default)
  top         most-used commands (first word of each exec)
  errors      per-command failure rates; prompt aborts (status 130) counted
              separately — they blame the previous command, not the failed one
  sessions    human vs agent shells (tty= flag when present, heuristic before)
  candidates  optimization candidates: repeated patterns, heavy hitters,
              bin/ tools with zero recorded use
  health      module source_failure counts (which conf.d modules fail, where)

Options:
  --days N    only consider events from the last N days (default: all)
  --top N     rows per table (default: 20)
  -h, --help  show this help
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
